+	/*!
+	 * The detected floor for SteamVR's room setup, as the Frame's HMD driver gives it
+	 * (docs/xr.md#room-setup): the dashboard announces each room-setup step to the drivers
+	 * (event 809, the step in data.u32[0]); in steps 3 (the boundary circle), 6 (the silent
+	 * floor detection at start) and 7 (the playspace setup) the floor's height in raw space goes,
+	 * through the room setup's transform, to vrserver (IVRServerInternal_XXX, vtable slot 40),
+	 * which hands it to the compositor ("floor_detection_result"): its floor target snaps to it
+	 * and accepting commits it. NaN clears it when the step ends. Each such step starts the
+	 * tracker's ground detection again, so the floor comes from what the head sees then.
